{"id": "EUVD-2026-93340", "enisaUuid": "a73565a5-3787-3d5c-a75d-b7dbe7daf6e2", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nRDMA/rtrs: guard against null kobj name\n\nIn the client, if `init_path()` errors, the callee tries to clean up\nwith `rtrs_clt_close_conns()`. However, this can lead to calling the\nevent tracing code with `clt_path->kobj->name` being `NULL` and thus\ncausing a null pointer dereference when trying to copy from it.\n\nThis just adds a guard to check that the name is not `NULL` before\ncopying from it. The server appears to have a similar pattern.", "datePublished": "2026-10-06T08:46:42", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:18:05", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f79cf42ff23f9120246cd6740eaa26f59c632a4a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/99c24a8968ebef0573825b5cb89d5985d51635b9"], "aliases": ["GHSA-w8vc-67qx-3qw3", "CVE-2026-98355"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.15, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "2a6f0f5c-7196-3f2c-b229-541120ea47bd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5a93929d9f9a1d82946ddd49e260b6dd1756ad6d <f79cf42ff23f9120246cd6740eaa26f59c632a4a"}, {"id": "65035045-5cdf-394c-96d5-2073027e8df4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "67acbf01-1374-31b5-88e6-9eaba4bf91fc", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.1"}, {"id": "71a608aa-1c65-3ec8-99fe-297a5cb46787", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.8"}, {"id": "b369eb33-db4f-3480-b8f6-ca989f9b8d70", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "f0fde383-4c18-3a1e-981a-7fd4dbff4cd5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5a93929d9f9a1d82946ddd49e260b6dd1756ad6d <99c24a8968ebef0573825b5cb89d5985d51635b9"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "8cc40a74-68fa-3e4a-9806-1c5013da063e", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}